#pragma once
#include "QuestRules.h"

namespace ARPG::Quests::Dialogue {
// Original expansion dialogue. Every entry follows the stable catalog ID; none is generated at runtime.
struct Conversation {const char *why,*hint,*ready;};
inline constexpr Conversation Conversations[] = {
 {"The little ones think everything with a flower is friendly. A Deku Baba rather spoils that lesson.","Look along our forest paths. Only the snapping plants here are the problem; leave the ordinary flowers alone.","No more snapping on the breakfast path? Let us find you something useful."},
 {"New shoots cannot drink a promise. Dewleaf keeps the soil around their roots damp.","Look for the green rings here in the forest. Stop beside each bundle long enough to gather it carefully.","You kept the stems whole! These will do nicely."},
 {"The Great Deku Tree has watched over us for as long as any of us remembers. Seeing him suffer makes the whole forest feel small.","If our guardian has called you inside, answer him. We cannot see what is happening beneath his bark.","You did everything you could. Come sit with us a moment."},
 {"These are ordinary trees. They cannot replace our guardian, but that does not mean we should stop caring for them.","Find the three marked beds in our forest. Clear the monsters away, then stand quietly in each ring while you plant.","Three new trees. Let us remember this as the day we began looking after something again."},
 {"A horse cannot explain why it refuses a road. Claw marks in the cart are rather easier to understand.","Look for the three Milk-road ambushers marked in Hyrule Field. Those are the ones troubling our route.","The driver can stop looking over his shoulder. Here, you have earned this."},
 {"Feed is meant to go in horses. Somehow that very simple arrangement has become terribly complicated.","Defeat the creatures carrying our pouches out in Hyrule Field. Six pouches should see the horses through.","Every pouch accounted for! I will try to get these past the horses without losing a sleeve."},
 {"When a horse is tired, you stop for it. People ought to be allowed the same kindness.","Gather the marked timber at the ranch first. Then find the three roadside work rings in Hyrule Field and build there.","I will keep the stations supplied. You have done the hardest part."},
 {"News travels with people. I would like someone to carry a kind piece of it for once.","Visit Kakariko and Lake Hylia while you are out. Seeing the roads for yourself will help us plan the next milk run.","Both roads checked? Then there is still a way to reach our neighbors."},
 {"Good rock has a flavor! Asking us to eat any old pebble is like asking you to eat your boots.","The marked red-ore seams are on Death Mountain Trail. Gather all three before coming back to the city.","That color! That crunch! Come here, little friend; you have saved supper."},
 {"Our food is inside that cavern. So are the things that would like to make food out of us.","Look for Dodongos and their little ones inside Dodongo's Cavern. Four will give the food carriers some breathing room.","Four fewer hungry mouths between us and dinner. A fine bit of work!"},
 {"We cannot keep living on scraps from the trail. Our cavern is our pantry, and we need it back.","Finish the trouble deep in Dodongo's Cavern. If you already helped Darunia, tell us when you are ready.","Our food supply is safe. A city that can eat is a city that can hope."},
 {"Carrying a sack of rocks in the dark is difficult. Carrying a sack of rocks after tripping over another rock is worse.","Repair the three marked braziers on the trail. Clear anything snapping at your heels before you begin.","The mountain path has its lights back. Let us send you away with a proper thank-you."},
 {"Those jumping creatures churn the shallows whenever a water bearer approaches.","Four Tektites along Zora's River. The ones elsewhere are not troubling this stretch of water.","The shallows can settle at last. Your help deserves more than a bow."},
 {"The pearls belong in the filters, where they trap the silt. We had not intended to test their usefulness inside monsters.","Search the creatures around Zora's Fountain. Five recovered pearls will repair the missing set.","All five! We shall clean these very thoroughly."},
 {"Lord Jabu-Jabu is precious to our people, and the princess has not returned. We have much to fear and little we can see.","Search within Lord Jabu-Jabu if you can gain entry. Bring an end to whatever is making him ill.","Our guardian is relieved of his sickness. We are in your debt."},
 {"The river carries what happens upstream to everyone below. We should leave our neighbors something better than silt.","Stand at each marked spring filter beside Zora's River and clear it. There are three that need your attention.","That current looks clearer already. Please accept our gratitude."},
 {"The birds cannot tell a harmless rustle from something dangerous. Lately I am not sure I can, either.","Look for restless creatures in the graveyard. Poes count too. Make sure you have cleared four before coming back.","Four fewer things scratching in the dark. Perhaps I can sleep as well as the birds."},
 {"Impa opened this village to people who needed a home. I can at least make sure there is somewhere to rest.","Find the three marked parcels here in Kakariko, then use the supplies at the three village work rings.","Nobody should have to ask twice for a blanket. Thank you for making that possible."},
 {"Someone has to ask after people who do not come home. The families should not have to walk that road alone.","The badges were lost on Death Mountain Trail. Clear six creatures there and recover what they carried.","You brought back all the badges. I will speak to the families myself."},
 {"I do not know every name on those stones. I still think somebody ought to notice when a light goes out.","Find the three marked memorials in the graveyard. Tend them without moving the stones.","You took care over each one. I could not ask for more."},
 {"Our paths used to be for games. Now we count everyone who comes back through the door.","Only the three marked Thornbound stalkers in the Lost Woods are part of this hunt. Find open ground and watch carefully.","All three are gone? Perhaps we can stop counting the footsteps outside."},
 {"Saria cared about this forest more than anybody. If she went to the temple, she must have had a reason.","Search the Forest Temple. We only know the trouble there has reached all the way to our homes.","The forest can breathe again. Whatever happened inside, you helped us."},
 {"The woods have good seeds left. We thought the meadow might be a kind place for them to start.","Gather the three seed bundles in the Lost Woods first, then plant at the three meadow work rings.","A little green beneath those old walls. That is a fine thing to leave behind."},
 {"Each family scratches its own mark on a meal token. Small things can tell us who has been through a terrible place.","The tokens were taken into the Fire Temple. Recover six from its monsters; do not risk a life for a seventh.","I recognize these marks. We can start putting them back where they belong."},
 {"Our people are not a dragon's supper. Darunia would never stand aside and let that happen.","Continue into the Fire Temple and stop Volvagia. The rescued Gorons can tell you more than anyone here.","The dragon is defeated. There will be time to grieve, and time to gather everyone close."},
 {"Some of us have come home to empty hearths. A warm meal and a neighbor are a good place to begin.","There are three marked relief stations here in Goron City. Rebuild them and we will bring the food.","Three places to eat together. You have understood what we needed."},
 {"Water, ice, creatures, weather: they all leave evidence. I cannot study a rumor under a lens.","The Ice Cavern is above Zora's Fountain. Look for three marked frost samples on safe ground inside.","Keep those samples separate! Excellent. Now we can ask a useful question."},
 {"The lake did not empty itself out of spite. Something has disturbed it, and the temple is where the evidence leads.","Investigate the Water Temple. A measuring stick cannot solve this part of the problem for me.","My lake has returned! Our next experiment may require a much longer measuring stick."},
 {"Water can return before everything that lives in it does. Recovery deserves a little patience.","Repair three marked filters along Lake Hylia's shore. Dry land near the water is quite sufficient; do not dive after a ring.","The filters are ready. Now we give the small creatures their chance."},
 {"The letter is old. Whoever wrote it wanted those belongings remembered, and I can understand that.","The journal records a narrow passage beneath the well, accessible to a child. The five keepsakes come from creatures below, not from the village.","Five keepsakes, and the chance to put names to them. Thank you for taking the letter seriously."},
 {"Impa has protected this village for so long. I cannot bear the thought of everyone simply waiting for her to do it alone.","Follow the trouble beneath the graveyard into the Shadow Temple. I cannot tell you what waits there.","That dreadful noise has stopped. Come here, before you hurry into another danger."},
 {"A light in a window says somebody is there. I want Kakariko to say that to everyone on the road.","Repair three marked village beacons. Give yourself a quiet moment at each one to finish the work.","I can see the next light from here. It makes the village feel a little less alone."},
 {"My crew can argue all day and still raise a beam together. I want every one of those fools back.","There are four carpenters held inside the fortress. Free the whole crew; they know their part of the bridge work.","Four workers home, one bridge rebuilt! Come collect your pay before I start shouting again."},
 {"A bridge gets people across. Tools and supplies give them a reason to make the journey.","Recover six tool rolls from monsters in Gerudo Valley, then rebuild the three marked valley supply stations.","That is a supply route I can work with. A proper job deserves proper pay."},
 {"The wasteland is dangerous even to those who know it. We do not leave our scouts to guess in a storm.","Keep to solid ground in the Haunted Wasteland. Repair three marked posts and reach the Desert Colossus using the normal crossing route.","You reached the far side and left signals behind. The next traveler has a better chance."},
 {"Power has made our temple a place of fear. Our people deserve better than obeying it without question.","Search the Spirit Temple and face the witches at its heart. What happened to Nabooru must be learned there.","The witches are defeated. That is a truth our people needed to hear."},
 {"It is easy to promise help to someone you see each morning. The distant neighbors matter too.","Visit Kokiri Forest, Goron City, and Zora's Domain. Even where wounds remain, the promise still matters.","You carried it to all three places. We will have to work hard to live up to those words."},
 {"People have set supplies aside for the journey to the castle. It is a small way to stand beside you.","Inside Ganon's Castle, defeat eight monsters and recover eight stolen relief seals. Other castles and towers are not the place.","The seals are back. I will make sure the supplies reach the people waiting for them."},
 {"I do not understand the magic you have described. I understand that you will need something to eat before facing what lies beyond it.","Clear all six trials inside Ganon's Castle. The journal records each broken barrier; come back before you climb the tower.","All six cleared? Then take what we have saved for you. Every little bit comes with someone's hope."},
 {"Waiting is easier when there is useful work to do. Those beacons are something all of us will be able to see.","Build the three marked beacons in Hyrule Field, then return here before you face the tower.","The lights are ready. So are your supplies. Let us send you on your way properly."},
 {"Saria's tune helps the woods feel familiar. We wondered whether a small, careful adventure could begin with it.","Learn the melody from Saria in the meadow if you do not know it. Play it freely in the Lost Woods, then inspect three forest patches by day.","You heard the echo and checked every patch. Next time we can explore without trampling the plants!"},
 {"We cannot go wandering out of the forest with parcels. You can carry a little kindness farther than we can.","Gather all three forest bundles, then speak to a Goron in Goron City and choose the delivery topic in your quest journal.","They have their leaves? Good. We will call that a successful trade, even if they tasted the wrapping."},
 {"My mother made the melody Epona loves. I think a familiar song can make a frightened creature feel at home.","Learn Epona's Song from me if you need to. Play it here, then return at night and stand still for twenty seconds. Moving or getting hurt restarts the watch.","Just a loose shutter? All that worry over a bit of wood! Thank you for listening."},
 {"Caring for an animal should not mean suffering every time you get close to it. Cleaner bedding might make her work a little easier.","Gather three bedding bundles here, then find the cucco keeper in Kakariko by day. Use the delivery topic when you are beside her.","Bedding delivered. I hope it makes tomorrow's chores kinder to her."},
 {"I nearly scrubbed the marks away before wondering whether somebody might know what they mean.","Examine the three marked graveyard stones in daylight. Then show your notes to the scientist inside the Lakeside Laboratory.","Useful marks, and every stone still in its place. A very satisfactory expedition."},
 {"The birds see a glimmer and begin shouting. I would like one explanation that does not end with me hiding under a blanket.","Enter the graveyard at night and check all three rings. Then play the Sun's Song there. The old royal tomb is tied to that melody.","Dew! I might have known the culprit would be something the cuccos could drink."},
 {"Our Big Brother likes a good tune. A drum would help the rest of us keep up, assuming we can stop thinking about lunch.","Play Saria's Song here in the city. Then inspect three marked ore seams on the trail by day. Tapping is enough; do not eat the evidence.","The best stone has a beautiful ring. Come, we owe our drum-finder a reward."},
 {"When the bell rings, we notice who is missing. That is a reason to keep ringing it, even when it hurts.","Inspect the three marked trail stone piles first. The three supper stands in Goron City can then be rebuilt.","The stands are sound. We can ring the bell and gather around it again."},
 {"A clear-looking river can still carry trouble. We want to help the people downstream before they have to ask.","Check three river filters by day, then three at night. Leave and return after the time changes if the sky stays still here. Take the notes to the laboratory.","Two sets of observations and an answer from the scientist. That is care worthy of the river."},
 {"A clean experiment needs a sound bottle. A Zora's eye for water will tell me more than another broken stopper ever could.","Speak to Malon at the ranch first, then a Zora in the domain. As an adult, King Zora must be thawed before he can receive anything.","Both opinions, written down in order! If only all my assistants were this careful."},
 {"The lake has water again, but the next shower will wash the shore into it. I would like to know what gets through.","Learn the Song of Storms from the windmill musician if needed. Play it at Lake Hylia, then inspect the three marked filters in daylight.","Your field notes are damp but legible. An excellent combination."},
 {"We cannot bring Saria to a place just by wishing. We can keep the place she loved peaceful.","Play Saria's Song in the meadow. Then stand still in daylight for thirty seconds without taking damage. There is no need to make the forest answer.","Thank you for taking the time. Sometimes that is the part people forget."},
 {"A badly checked joint waits until everyone trusts it. That is when it breaks. We are going to be boringly thorough.","Inspect all three valley timber stacks by day, ask a fortress guard for the crossing report, then repair the three valley approach lights.","The guard agrees, the timber is checked, and the signals work. Even I am running out of complaints."},
 {"A post leaning into the wind tells you something. So does sand piling on its sheltered side. Learn before you hurry.","Inspect three marked wasteland posts, then stand still on solid ground for twenty seconds without taking damage. Move to safety first if a creature approaches.","You observed instead of guessing. Keep that habit when nobody is paying you for it."},
 {"We can guard a water jar. Knowing how to keep its contents fit to drink calls for a different skill.","Get the scientist's advice inside the lake laboratory before collecting three marked lakeshore herb bundles. Return them to a fortress guard through the delivery topic.","Advice, supplies, and a traveler who kept their word. A fair exchange."},
 {"Fear does not leave the moment a monster does. A quiet night is something people have to learn to trust again.","Check three village lanterns at night, then stand still and unharmed for thirty seconds. Finally mend the three remembrance lights here.","Nothing dreadful happened. That is the finest report you could have brought me."},
 {"A supper can begin long before anyone sits down. Sometimes it begins with making sure a neighbor knows they were invited.","Find a Kokiri outdoors in the restored forest first, then a Goron in Goron City. The invitations are delivery topics in your journal.","Both greetings delivered! I will find a table strong enough for Goron hospitality."},
 {"I cannot promise a happy ending. I can promise there will be people here who want to see one with you.","Visit the head carpenter outside in Gerudo Valley, then a fortress guard, then Malon at the ranch. Ask each through the delivery topic and return to Kakariko.","They all said yes? Then we have something wonderful to prepare while we wait for you."},
};
static_assert(std::size(Conversations)==ARPG_QUEST_COUNT);
inline const Conversation& For(int id) {return Conversations[(Find(id)?id:1)-1];}
// Actual named actors select a voice. Generic residents never impersonate their leaders.
enum class Voice { Kokiri, Mido, Saria, Malon, Goron, Darunia, Zora, KingZora, CuccoKeeper, Scientist, Carpenter, Gerudo };
inline const char* Name(Voice v) {
    constexpr const char* names[]={"Kokiri villager","Mido","Saria","Malon","Goron","Darunia","Zora resident","King Zora","Cucco keeper","Lakeside scientist","Head carpenter","Gerudo guard"};
    return names[int(v)];
}
inline const char* Greeting(Voice v,bool adult,uint32_t story) {
    switch(v) {
        case Voice::Mido:return adult?(story&Forest?"The woods are quieter. If you see a boy called Link... never mind. There is work we can do here.":"I made a promise to Saria. If you want to help this forest, you had better mean it."):"I am keeping an eye on things! You can help, if you follow through for once.";
        case Voice::Saria:return "There you are! Take a breath. You always seem ready to run somewhere. Shall we talk?";
        case Voice::Malon:return adult?"Come over here a moment. A friendly face makes the chores feel lighter.":"Hello, fairy boy! Mind your pockets. The horses are hoping you brought something tasty.";
        case Voice::Darunia:return "Stand tall, little friend! A good heart is worth more than a big pair of fists. What brings you here?";
        case Voice::Goron:return adult?(story&Fire?"Good to hear footsteps coming home to the city. Have you eaten?": "The city is too quiet. I keep listening for our people on the stairs."):"Come close! We were just discussing supper. It is a very serious subject.";
        case Voice::Zora:return "Welcome, traveler. Those who care for the river are welcome to speak here.";
        case Voice::KingZora:return adult?"Our troubles have not all melted away, but I will hear you, traveler.":"Speak, traveler. The well-being of my people and my daughter weighs upon me.";
        case Voice::CuccoKeeper:return adult?"Oh, hello! For once, that noise was only a cucco. What a relief.":"Please step around the birds. I love them dearly, even when they make me sneeze.";
        case Voice::Scientist:return "A visitor! Have you brought an observation, a question, or something leaking?";
        case Voice::Carpenter:return story&Carpenters?"The bridge is standing and the crew is working. Miracles do happen. What do you need?":"If you have seen my crew, speak up! A foreman cannot build a bridge out of worry.";
        case Voice::Gerudo:return story&Spirit?"You have kept your word before. I will hear what you have to say.":"You may speak. Be clear, and respect the people who live here.";
        default:return adult?(story&Forest?"Hello, mister! It is good to hear the birds over the monsters again.":"Keep your voice low, mister. We are waiting for the paths to be safe."):"Want to hear what is happening around the forest? There is always something!";
    }
}
enum class Stage : uint8_t { Offer, Why, Hint, Ready, Thanks };
inline const char* Line(int id,Stage stage,Voice voice) {
    if(voice==Voice::Saria && id==41) {
        if(stage==Stage::Offer)return "Try playing my melody in the Lost Woods. Then look for three sunlit dewleaf patches back here. We can learn which little plants the forest is keeping safe.";
        if(stage==Stage::Why)return "A familiar tune can help you feel less lost. I thought a small, careful adventure could begin with mine.";
        if(stage==Stage::Hint)return "If you still need to learn my melody, meet me in the Sacred Forest Meadow. Play it freely in the Lost Woods, then inspect three forest patches by day.";
    }
    const auto* d=Find(id);if(!d)return "";const auto& c=For(id);
    switch(stage) {case Stage::Offer:return d->offer;case Stage::Why:return c.why;case Stage::Hint:return c.hint;case Stage::Ready:return c.ready;case Stage::Thanks:return d->thanks;}
    return "";
}
inline const char* DeliveryReply(int id,int objective) {
    switch(id) {
        case 42:return "Leaves for wrapping? Ah! That explains the flavor. Tell the forest folk we are grateful.";
        case 44:return "Clean bedding from Malon! That is so thoughtful. Please tell her the birds and I both thank her.";
        case 45:return "These grooves record water levels. No buried treasure, I am afraid. Tell her to compare their surface after dark.";
        case 49:return "Day and night, carefully compared! Silt is drifting down after sunset. Tell the Zoras when to clean those filters.";
        case 50:return objective==0?"A stopper, and absolutely no milk in the bottle. There! Tell him I followed his very stern instructions.":"The sample is cloudy, but the seal is sound. I have noted the sediment for the scientist. Please carry back our observations.";
        case 53:return "The crossing is holding. Our patrol noted three dark approach posts; I have marked them on the report. Give your foreman that.";
        case 55:return objective==0?"Use the lakeshore leaves to line the covers, and keep the jars shaded. I have marked suitable bundles outside. Clean water deserves a clean journey.":"Three bundles, and his instructions. Our scouts will make good use of both. Your task here is done.";
        case 57:return objective==0?"We cannot come out of our forest, but please give Malon our good wishes. It is nice to be remembered.":"A supper invitation! We will bring rocks for our own plates. Tell Malon we know the milk is for drinking, not seasoning.";
        case 58:return objective==0?"Benches? Of course! Tell her I will make them sturdy enough for whoever turns up.":objective==1?"We can spare water jars. Tell the village a promise from us will arrive filled.":"Supper for everyone? I will do what I can. Tell her to save a place for you, fairy boy.";
        default:return "I have your message. Thank you for bringing it yourself.";
    }
}
}
